    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family C). Consolidates F38.B4 (filed on WI-bupim) + F39.C2 (filed on INV-bazij), with cross-substrate confirmation on max10 / ROOT / HTRAC. Full evidence remains on the parent discussion entries; this row provides discrete representation as a structurally-distinct INV-bazij mechanism — sibling to WI-bupim's typed-tier and WI-sirid's markdown-occurrence-index.\n\n## Symptom\n\nThe TypeScript analyzer's stable_id hash inputs are insufficient to disambiguate distinct named symbols. 4 stable_ids each collapse 2-4 TypeScript symbols with **different `.name` values** to identical IDs:\n\n| stable_id (prefix) | Colliding symbols |\n|---|---|\n| `sha256:f4a7af6e179e8aba` | `{connect, connectWebSocket, registerServiceWorker, scheduleReconnect}` across 2 files |\n| `sha256:5b1252b57e00fd12` | `{ItemDetail.render, ItemList.render, TrackerApp.render}` across 3 Lit component files |\n| `sha256:465a58dbfa932b3a` | `{ItemDetail.onDiscussSubmit, TrackerApp.connectedCallback, ItemDetail.onBack, TrackerApp.onBack}` |\n| `sha256:e067b2ec87edc43c` | `{ItemDetail.onStatusChange, ItemDetail.onDiscussInput}` |\n\nStructurally different from prior INV-bazij cohorts: this is NOT name-repetition (bash export-VAR) or placeholder (kafka/graphql) or parse-artifact (SQL parsing). It's distinct-named symbols collapsing because the hash inputs exclude name+path+span+class disambiguation. Hash inputs in `js_ts.py` are insufficient for TS function+method nodes.\n\n## Cross-substrate scope (production-scale)\n\nThe 4 TS clusters are present in ROOT default substrate per pass-38 F38.B6 — NOT a truncation artifact. They surface as collisions when the substrate is small enough that the denominator doesn't mask them.\n\nUpdated INV-bazij cross-substrate matrix (snapshot from passes 38-39):\n\n| Codebase | Nodes | Rate | Dominant cohort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ROOT default | 34253 | 0.84% | mixed (this cohort masked) |\n| TRACKER | 4959 | 0.81% | python residual |\n| SCRIPTS default | 416 | 7.0% **BREACH** | bash export-VAR (WI-bash-export-symbol-dedup) |\n| **HTRAC default** | **77** | **16.88% BREACH** | **TS hash-input bug (this row)** |\n| CLI_PKG | 32 | 0.00% | — |\n| DOCS default | 2861 | 0.38% | markdown within-file-dup-heading (WI-sirid) |\n\nHTRAC's 16.88% breach is entirely from these 4 TS hash-input bug clusters: 13/77 colliding nodes = exactly the F38.B4 cohort. Three substrates (max10 + ROOT default + HTRAC) independently confirm the same 4 collision groups.\n\n**This is a SECOND INV-bazij DEFAULT-mode breach** after the SCRIPTS breach (pass-38 F38.D3 / WI-bash-export-symbol-dedup, the other Family C row).\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor the TypeScript analyzer, the stable_id hash input for function/method symbol kinds must incorporate sufficient disambiguators that distinct symbols (different `.name` AND/OR different `.path` AND/OR different enclosing-class context) produce distinct stable_ids with negligible (cryptographic) collision probability.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nExtend the stable_id hash construction in `js_ts.py` for TS function/method nodes to include `name + qualified_name + path + span` — paralleling the Python analyzer fix that landed during INV-bazij Phase 6 PR3 (commit `ea0154e54f`, name+qualified_name hash inputs at `compute_stable_id` / `py.py::_compute_stable_id`). The same kind of mechanical sweep WI-bupim describes for typed-tier callers applies here, but the failure mode is different (cross-name collapse, not within-name repetition), so the fix-input set is different. js_ts.py joins WI-bupim's typed-tier callers cohort but with cross-name as the mechanism.\n\nPre-condition for fix: confirm whether the missing input is `name` (most likely) or `qualified_name` or `class_context` (or all three). Top candidate cluster (`{connect, ...}`) all 4 names are textually distinct so the missing input must include `.name`. Fix probably needs all of name+path+span+class.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F38.B4** — WI-bupim discussion entry 2026-06-02T22:15:54 (pass-38 batch; see paragraph beginning \"F38.B4: NEW BUG — TypeScript analyzer hash-input-insufficient cross-name collision\").\n- **F39.C2** — INV-bazij discussion entry 2026-06-02T22:52:36 (pass-39 batch; \"F39.C2 SECOND DEFAULT-mode breach + TS hash-input cohort cross-substrate verification\" — 3-substrate verification: max10 + ROOT default + HTRAC).\n\nLab notebooks: passes 38, 39 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-bazij** (META: stable_id mass collisions) — sibling under same parent to WI-bupim and WI-sirid.\n- Sibling: **WI-bupim** (typed-tier name disambiguation across 10 analyzers — analogous fix-path family, different analyzer surface; the audit suggests WI-bupim's residual scope expand to MULTI-MECHANISM, with this row breaking out the TS sub-mechanism for independent triage).\n- Sibling: **WI-bash-export-symbol-dedup** (Family C — bash within-name repetition; OTHER INV-bazij DEFAULT-mode breach; same INV-bazij scope but different language/mechanism).\n- Sibling: **WI-sirid-markdown-stable-id-occurrence-index** (Family B — INV-bazij 6th mechanism).\n- Cousin row: WI-vodin (canonical id-format static check) — same META cluster INV-tazaj."  # a342
